# Force non-www canonical. Fixes Google Search Console "Duplicate without
# user-selected canonical" indexing issue identified June 10, 2026.
# Any request to www.gebauerwatches.com 301s to the non-www canonical.
https://www.gebauerwatches.com/* https://gebauerwatches.com/:splat 301!
http://www.gebauerwatches.com/*  https://gebauerwatches.com/:splat 301!
http://gebauerwatches.com/*      https://gebauerwatches.com/:splat 301!

# /blog retired Aug 1 2026. The route was removed from main.jsx, so without
# these rules the SPA would render the homepage at /blog, which is a soft 404
# and Google treats those as a quality problem. A 301 tells crawlers the pages
# are gone and moves any existing link equity to the homepage.
# Substack is the publication. See gebauer-site/src/posts.js for the archive.
/blog/*  /  301
/blog    /  301

# /specs retired Aug 17 2026. The specification table now lives inline under
# the watches on the homepage - one page instead of sending people to a second
# one. The URL is kept alive because it is in llms.txt and was mailed out.
/specs   /#watches   301
/specs/  /#watches   301
